vious player is: Play T3, Play W2, Play W3, Play B4, Play W6, Play W6, Play W1, Play W4, Gang J1, Play B9, Play B1, Play T2, Play J2, Play F4, Peng B2, Play B3, Play T1, Play J2, Peng B3, Play B6, Play B6, Play T8, Play W7, Play T5.\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Chi T4; Pass]\u3002", "reasoning": "", "output": "Evaluation: Let me analyze the current situation and valid actions:\n\n**Current Hand Analysis:**\n- Hand tiles: [T2: 2; T3: 1; T4: 1; T7: 3; B7: 2; B8: 2; B9: 2]\n- This is 13 tiles total: T2, T2, T3, T4, T7, T7, T7, B7, B7, B8, B8, B9, B9\n\n**Valid Actions:**\n1. **Chi T4** - This means I can form a Chow [T3, T4, T5] by claiming a T5 just discarded by the previous player\n2. **Pass** - Do nothing\n\n**Analysis of Chi T4:**\n\nIf I Chi T4 (claiming T5 to form [T3, T4, T5]):\n- Remaining hand: T2, T2, T7, T7, T7, B7, B7, B8, B8, B9, B9 (11 tiles)\n- Exposed meld: [T3, T4, T5]\n- This gives me:\n  - T7 pung (T7, T7, T7) \n  - Potential B7-B8-B9 chow\n  - A pair of T2s, B7s, B8s, or B9s\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Looking at the game history of the previous player, the last action was \"Play T5\", so they discarded T5. The valid action \"Chi T4\" with my tiles would form the chow [T3, T4, T5].\n\n**Evaluating Chi T4:**\n- After Chi: Hand becomes T2, T2, T7, T7, T7, B7, B7, B8, B8, B9, B9\n- I have T7 pung (concealed)\n- I have potential for B7-B8-B9 straight\n- I need one more meld and a pair\n\nHowever, forming an exposed meld limits my ability to score high-value patterns like \"Fully Concealed Hand\" (4 pts) or \"Concealed Hand\" (2 pts). \n\n**Current Potential Patterns:**\n- All Simples (2 pts) - currently all tiles are simples\n- The hand is not close to any high-value patterns\n\n**Unshown Tiles Analysis:**\n- T5: only 1 remaining (I'd be taking it)\n- B6: 2 remaining (needed for B7-B8-B9 \u2192 B6-B7-B8 flexibility)\n- Many tiles still available\n\nThe Chi doesn't significantly improve my winning chances and sacrifices concealment points. My 