7 pung as anchor\n\nReason: W3 is an isolated tile that doesn't contribute to any meld formation. Discarding it maintains my T7 concealed pung, preserves the T2-T3-T4 chow potential, and keeps all my valuable pairs in the Dots suit (B7-B7, B8-B8, B9-B9). This gives me the best flexibility to pursue either a Seven Pairs pattern or a standard winning hand with multiple scoring patterns like \"All Pungs\" or \"Half Flush\" (if I draw more Dots/Bamboo tiles).\n\nAnswer: Play W3"}
